{"availability":"available","full":"Phoenix6001/SmartZoom","name":"SmartZoom","description":"macOS smart zoom for Windows: press a mouse button or shortcut and the paragraph, image or table under the cursor fills the window; press again to snap back. Works in Chromium browsers, Firefox, Word, Excel and PDF readers with no extensions. Tray app, .NET 10, MIT.","category":"Productivity","language":"C#","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-24T07:05:34Z","updated":"2026-10-07T13:04:25Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://smartzoom.pages.dev","topics":["accessibility","dotnet","low-vision","magnifier","productivity","smart-zoom","tray-app","windows","wpf","zoom"],"demo":"https://smartzoom.pages.dev/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:07.974Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:07.974Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:07.974Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T14:48:07.974Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Bringing macOS's smart zoom to Windows. Press a mouse button and the application under the cursor zooms its content in on whatever you are pointing at, and brings it to the middle of the window — by the amount you choose in a browser, or to fit the paragraph, table or block of cells in Word and Excel. Press again to return to exactly where you were.","Website: smartzoom.pages.dev · Download: SmartZoom-setup.exe (always the latest release)","Windows has no system gesture for this, so SmartZoom is a small tray app that captures a mouse or keyboard trigger and routes it to a per-application zoom strategy:"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Phoenix6001/SmartZoom/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f5e644e39ca77c4a789bd545310bb45e892528fb117ae9fcd3dd3f419fd968a0","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:08.130Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:08.130Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Bringing macOS's smart zoom to Windows. Press a mouse button and the application under the cursor zooms its content in on whatever you are pointing at, and brings it to the middle of the window — by the amount you choose in a browser, or to fit the paragraph, table or block of cells in Word and Excel. Press again to return to exactly where you were.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Phoenix6001/SmartZoom/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The wizard offers to start SmartZoom when you sign in, which is on by default because a zoom trigger that stops working at the next sign-out is not much use.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Phoenix6001/SmartZoom/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"f5e644e39ca77c4a789bd545310bb45e892528fb117ae9fcd3dd3f419fd968a0","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Phoenix6001/SmartZoom/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:08.130Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T13:04:25Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Phoenix6001/SmartZoom/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:08.131Z","hash":"f5e644e39ca77c4a789bd545310bb45e892528fb117ae9fcd3dd3f419fd968a0","originalBytes":22249,"storedBytes":22249,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["zoom","smartzoom","docs","what","press","page","window","one","settings","which","button","mouse","windows","every","left","back","exactly","same","smart","trigger","word","does","excel","gesture","pinch","reader","application","browser","cursor","own","about","app","keys","middle","strategy","change","click","ctrl","ctrl+wheel","diagnostics","double-tap","exact","file","how","nothing","only","pdf","rather","readers","second","tapcount","true","under","block","ctrlwheel","log","modifiers","needs","presses","report","still","them","through","touch","when","works","zooms","already","amount","bare","because","blocks","browsers","build","code","default","double-click","each","first","fit","install","installer","never","off","once","out","pointed","re